{"reference":"Zechariah 2","book":"Zechariah","chapter":2,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"The Measuring Vision","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The measuring of Jerusalem introduces a vision of a city so populous that it is described as open like unwalled villages. Its security is not portrayed as resting on ordinary walls: the Lord promises to be a protecting “wall of fire” around it and to dwell within it. The summons to flee from the north and from Babylon belongs to this same vision of gathering and protection.","verse_refs":["Zechariah 2:1-13"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_zechariah_002_91de9bd0854258fc1a4c66b6"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}